> 
>  res.nnet <- CVtest(
> +     function(x, ...) nnet(quality~nmsr1+nmsr2, proeve[x,], ...),
> +     function(obj, x) predict(obj, proeve[x,], type="class"),
> size=3,weights=w, maxit=200,skip=T, entropy= T, trace=F)
> fold1
> Error in fitfn(rand != i, size = 3, weights = ..2, maxit = 200, skip = ..4,
> entro..: Object "..2" not found
> Dumped

It is a scope problem (w does not exist wehn you need it), but in any case
this will not work (you want the weights for the subset, not the whole
set).  Try

>  res.nnet <- CVtest(
> +     function(x, ...) nnet(quality~nmsr1+nmsr2, proeve[x,],
weights=proeve[x, "w"], ...),
> +     function(obj, x) predict(obj, proeve[x,], type="class"),
> size=3,maxit=200,skip=T, entropy= T, trace=F)

or perhaps better

function(x, ...) nnet(quality~nmsr1+nmsr2, proeve, weights=w, subset=x, ...)

if I understand your intentions correctly.

