Subject: [S] cross-validation of neural network performance
Message-ID: <48E83DF309C0D211B1FB0060970CF8AD028E8A@DMUKN3>

Dear S-Plussers

I would be interested to hear your opinion about cross-validation of neural
network models.

The challenge I see is that neural networks often have several local minima
solutions to the same set of data, some of which are far from the best solution.

When I do 10-fold cross-validation, I get an average-performance including both
good and bad local minima solutions.

Now:
Is it reasonable to consider stable models with a few local minima of comparable
good fit superior to unstable models with frequent poor local minima and
occassional good fits?

Or should I rather compare the best local minima of competing models and neglect
the inferior solutions?

Is there a better way?

regards

