From rolf at math.unb.ca  Wed Dec  1 15:33:49 1999
From: rolf at math.unb.ca (Rolf Turner)
Date: Wed, 01 Dec 1999 11:33:49 -0400
Subject: [S] GLMMs.
Message-ID: <199912011533.LAA28076@tanner.math.unb.ca>

In a recent posting Prof. Brian Ripley wrote:

>                                                    There is not much
>  software around to fit GLMMs in S, although for some specific GLMMs
>  some does exist.

Murray Aitkin has written software in GLIM4 to analyze generalized
linear mixed models, with the emphasis being on modelling
overdispersion through random effects.  The ideas are discussed in
his paper in ``A general maximum likelihood analysis of
overdispersion in generalized linear models'', Statistics and
Computing, vol. 6, 1996, pp. 251-262.

The GLIM4 macros to implement the ideas can be found at the URLs

http://www.mas.ncl.ac.uk/~nma9/allvc.txt   (variance component macro)
http://www.mas.ncl.ac.uk/~nma9/alldist.txt  (overdispersion macro)

It might well be a useful exercise for someone who speaks both GLIM
and Splus (does such a person exist?) to translate Prof. Aitkin's
software into Splus.

                                        cheers,

                                                Rolf Turner
