Bert Gunter discovered, through this list, that the presence of row names
greatly increased the execution times for tapply(), one of the most critical
functions in Splus.  We had noted here that the same script, using moderately
large objects, ran *much* slower in Splus 5.1 than in 3.4, and the reason
was the execution of tapply().

Consider the following involving the vector fco2.hf, which is a column stripped
from a matrix and selected with a logical vector lzu.  It was created
using Splus 5.1 and 3.4 with identical scripts and has about 100,000 elements:

Version 5.1 Release 1 for Silicon Graphics Irix, IRIX 6.2 : 1999 
Working data will be in /users/strat/scw/MySwork 
> x1.0<-tapply(fco2.hf[lzu],iind[lzu],mean, na.rm = T) 
#takes 15 minutes
> names(fco2.hf)[1:10]
 [1] "" "" "" "" "" "" "" "" "" ""
> names(fco2.hf)<-NULL
> x1.0<-tapply(fco2.hf[lzu],iind[lzu],mean, na.rm = T) 
