Version 3.4 Release 1 for Silicon Graphics Iris, IRIX 5.3 : 1996 
Working data will be in /users/strat/scw/.SGIData 
> names(fco2.hf)[1:10]
NULL

Thus the vector fco2.hf has a (useless blank) set of names when created in
Splus 5.1, but a null set when using 3.4.  The names were null in
Splus 2000 and tapply ran fine there in this case.

The execution of tapply in the case with blank names took 15 minutes
in Splus 5.1. It took about 15 seconds when the names attribute was NULL, in
both 5.1 and 3.4.

Thus:  suggest users of Splus strip names from your objects in the first 
argument
of tapply until Mathsoft fixes
the underlying problem (definitely bug category) in tapply.

