Subject: [S] Object hidden within function.
Message-ID: <85256842.00619888.00@mail.spgdag.com>

Hello S-users,

I am trying to write a litte function which will extract a column from a
data.frame, sounds simple!
Here it is.

I would like to allow for the argument "component" to be either the column
number, the column off the data.frame itself (i.e. dfr$component), the quoted
name of the column or the unquoted name of the column.  The function works fine
when called from the command line but not when called from a function.  I can't
figure out the problem.  I would prefer not to have to assign "component" and I
definitely don't want to assign "dfr" as this is often a very large data.frame
and assigning it takes to much time.

function(dfr, component)
{
#  component : the column to extract from 'dfr'.  Note that component could be
#              of the form: "dfr$component", component(a name without quotes),
#              "component"(quoted) or component(a column number).

     what <- substitute(component)
     if(!is.name(what) & !is.character(what) & !is.numeric(what))
          what <- component
     else if (is.numeric(what))
          what <- dfr[,component]
        else
          what <- dfr[[as.character(what)]]
     what
}

Thanks to all,

