I have been living with this problem for several years.  My simple
solution allowing a single home directory is to have a subdirectory 
for S for the non-default machine.  I occasionally forget where I 
am, but S is good enough to remind me on startup with messages of 
the form

Warning messages:
  S-PLUS object(?) ".First" has unknown mode (0x2d010000) -- it does not look
        like an S-PLUS object made on this machine

If I had a choice, I'd stick to a single architecture.  

