From Kris.Angelovski at CMIS.CSIRO.AU  Fri Dec 10 04:18:40 1999
From: Kris.Angelovski at CMIS.CSIRO.AU
Date: Fri, 10 Dec 1999 15:18:40 +1100
Subject: [S] Courses in S-PLUS & XGobi - (Australia) February 2000
Message-ID: <01C5711ED0DCD111A3D70000F8077C6CCEAC28@parramatta.nsw.cmis.CSIRO.AU>

Two courses of interest to S-PLUS users and other data analysts will be held
in February 2000 by CSIRO at Macquarie University in Sydney:

*** Data Analysis and Graphics in S-PLUS, presented by Bill Venables
and
*** Interactive and Dynamic Graphical Data Exploration, presented by Di Cook
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
----------------------------

*** Data Analysis and Graphics in S-PLUS (3 days, 14 - 16 February) ***

Presented by Bill Venables, who recently joined the Environmetrics Group in
CSIRO Mathematical and Information Sciences after many years as a senior
lecturer at the University of Adelaide.  Bill is an experienced lecturer in
Statistics, internationally known S-PLUS expert, and co-author of the widely
used book Modern Applied Statistics with S-Plus, and soon to be released S
Programming.  Most people who use S-PLUS will know of Bill, and many will
have seen his comprehensive and enlightening solutions to questions on the
s-news group.

The course is predominantly in the use of the S-PLUS code, and not in the
S-PLUS for Windows GUI.
*       Who will benefit:   
People who have already used S-PLUS, but feel they could be getting more out
if it. This course will introduce you to many programming techniques and
tools or enhance your existing skills.
*       Includes:  
Overview of data types, interactive calculation, data manipulation, writing
functions, introduction to modelling, graphical functions, building graphs,
interactive graphics, session management.
*       Recommended Prerequisites:  
Some previous experience in using S-PLUS.  Please note that the course is
not intended as an introductory statistics course.  We shall assume that all
course participants have an elementary knowledge of statistics, and are
familiar with either the Unix or Windows operating system.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
----------------------------

*** Interactive and Dynamic Graphical Data Exploration (1 day, 17 February)
***

An introductory course in exploratory data analysis with dynamic graphics.
Presented by Dianne Cook, Associate Professor of Statistics at Iowa State
University.  She is an active researcher in interactive and dynamic
visualisation methods for data analysis, and teaches graduate and
undergraduate courses in multivariate analysis, exploratory data analysis,
and statistical methods.  Di is an author of the XGobi software, used for
exploratory data analysis and high-dimensional data visualisation.  She has
also been experimenting with the use of highly immersive virtual reality
environments for visualising multivariate spatially referenced data.  In the
past two years she has given several workshops in the United States on
interactive and dynamic graphics for data analysis using XGobi.

More information on XGobi is available at
http://www.research.att.com/~andreas/xgobi/index.html.  XGobi can be called
from S-PLUS, but it also operates as an independent product in its own
right.

*       Who will benefit:  
People who want to explore and model data.  This course will introduce you
to interactive (direct manipulation) and dynamic graphics approaches. Also,
instructors and students of multivariate statistical analysis and data
mining will learn of new methods for visualising multi-dimensional data.
*       Includes: 
Introduction to new visualisation methods, and an overview of graphics for
multi-dimensional data available on the desktop today, exploring the
distribution of missing values, clustering and classification, working with
compositional data, space/time variables, multivariate longitudinal data,
and what to do when you have large amounts of data.
*       Recommended Prerequisites: 
Some previous experience in data analysis.  Although but some knowledge of
it will be useful, it is not necessary to have used S-PLUS.  We shall assume
that all course participants have an elementary knowledge of statistics, and
are familiar with either the Unix or Windows operating system.

Full costs - but everyone can qualify for a discount!

Data Analysis and Graphics in S-PLUS            $1500  
Interactive and Graphical Data Exploration        $500  
Both courses (booked at the same time)          $1900

Discounts available:
*       10% discount  for customers in the CSIRO S-PLUS Annual Maintenance
Program
*       10% discount for bookings of 3 people or more from the same
organisation
*       Bookings made before 14 January 2000 will qualify for a $50 early
bird rebate

For example, an S-PLUS customer who is part of the CSIRO Maintenance Program
who books into both courses before 14 January can bring the total cost down
to $1660.  If three people from the same organisation attend, the cost
reduces even further to $1470/person.

