Message-ID: <Pine.HPX.4.10.9912131121550.18530-100000@rzsrv1.rz.tu-bs.de>

Dear Patrik,

On Mon, 13 Dec 1999, Patrik Ohagen wrote:

>   Each subject start at the same dose. If the response to that dose is 
>   satisfactory they receive no more doses. If not they proceed at the 
>   next dose level.

If you observe the event "response" for each patient a logistic regression
would do 

glm(response ~ Time + other.vars ,familily=binomial,link=logit). 

If you don't observe all events & you assume that each patient will
response in the infinite future you need to run survival-analyses.

> library(survival5)
> x<-data.frame(Event=c(1,1,1,0,1,1,0,0,0,0),Time=1:10)
> survfit(Surv(Time,Event),x)

The data required structure would be:

Time event
12    1
32    1 
43    0

