Subject: [S] Trellis margins
Message-ID: <199912141217.AA293603852@kria.lif.hi.is>

The trick to handle the margins around trellis figure, when they are
to be incorporated into LaTeX, is to save the figure when it is
first printed as EPS file, because the later printout has the 
large unwanted margin. Here is how it goes:

> trellis.device(postscript, color=F, file="myfigure.eps", onefile=F, 
> print.it=F)

> print(xyplot(...), position=c(0,0,1, 0.5))#for example
 
Starting to make postscript file.
Generated postscript file "myfigure.eps".
> unix("mv myfigure.eps myfigure.bak.eps")# save the "right" figure
character(0)
> dev.off()
Starting to make postscript file.
Generated postscript file "myfigure.eps".
 motif 
     2
> 

But this is just a trick that bypasses the real problem
of handling the margins more efficiently. Thanks to 
Andreas Krause and Henrik Nielsen for their suggestions.

Bjarki Eldon
