my avice is to always make sure your arguments are of the right type
and not to depend upon such function as is.xxx or as.xxx whose
behaviour is sometimes strange.

see for example:

> attributes(as.vector(list(a=0,b=1)))
$names:
[1] "a" "b"

although as.vector is supposed to strip its argument of any attribute.

e.e.

